    <p class="tag">Specialised Service</p>
    <h1>Exit Clearance &amp; Departure Requirements</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Confirm what you need before you leave the Philippines, not at the departure gate.</p>

    <p>Foreign nationals who have stayed in the Philippines for an extended period, or who hold certain long-term visas, may need to obtain clearance from the Bureau of Immigration before departing. FIS can confirm what applies to your departure, prepare the required documentation, and manage the appropriate clearance process before you travel.</p>

    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Confirming whether an exit clearance applies to your departure and which type is required</li>
      <li>Identifying any immigration matter that needs to be addressed before departure</li>
      <li>Preparing and organising the required documentation</li>
      <li>Managing and coordinating the clearance application with the Bureau of Immigration</li>
      <li>Coordinating connected immigration requirements, such as an outstanding extension or visa downgrade, before you depart</li>
      <li>Following up and keeping you informed as your departure approaches</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Common Situations We Handle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Departing after a long-term stay in the Philippines</li>
      <li>Holding a long-term visa and travelling temporarily, with plans to return</li>
      <li>Needing to resolve an outstanding immigration matter before leaving</li>
      <li>Preparing to depart where your immigration history or current status makes the requirements unclear</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the Process Works</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Initial enquiry</h3>
        <p>Tell us your current immigration status and travel plans.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Assessment</h3>
        <p>We confirm whether a clearance applies to your departure and which type is required.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Preparation</h3>
        <p>We prepare and organise the documentation required for your clearance.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Submission and follow-up</h3>
        <p>We manage and coordinate the clearance application, follow up as your departure approaches and keep you informed. You can track the progress of your transaction through the FIS Client Portal.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="service-cta">
      <h2>Confirm Your Departure Requirements</h2>
      <p>Tell us your travel plans and current immigration status. FIS will confirm what applies to your departure and manage the appropriate clearance process for you.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/?service=exit-clearance">Request Exit Clearance Assistance</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need an exit clearance every time I leave?</summary>
        <p>It depends on your immigration status, length of stay and the circumstances of your departure. Tell us your situation and FIS will confirm what applies to your upcoming travel.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What if I've overstayed and need to leave?</summary>
        <p>This is a common and manageable situation. Tell us your current immigration status and travel plans. FIS can assess what needs to be addressed before departure and coordinate the required immigration work in the appropriate order.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

